From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jordan Bettcher <thebettcher@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 09:10:46 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] [ppc64] runtime: build analyze_snapshot for ppc64

build_analyze_snapshot (runtime/runtime_args.gni) listed only x64, arm64
and riscv64, so runtime/bin:analyze_snapshot did not exist for ppc64 and
Flutter's //flutter:flutter could not depend on it. The tool needs a
64-bit AOT runtime, which ppc64 has; it builds unchanged and analyses an
app-aot-elf snapshot from the ppc64 gen_snapshot.
---
 runtime/runtime_args.gni | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/runtime/runtime_args.gni b/runtime/runtime_args.gni
index a246292a..7e68235d 100644
--- a/runtime/runtime_args.gni
+++ b/runtime/runtime_args.gni
@@ -101,7 +101,7 @@ declare_args() {
   # The analyze_snapshot tool is only supported on 64 bit AOT builds.
   build_analyze_snapshot =
       dart_target_arch == "x64" || dart_target_arch == "arm64" ||
-      dart_target_arch == "riscv64"
+      dart_target_arch == "riscv64" || dart_target_arch == "ppc64"
 }
 
 if (is_fuchsia) {
